### Phase 3.1: Profile Update Tests

### Test 1: Register User
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Saman",
  "lastName": "Perera",
  "email": "saman@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Test 2: Login User
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "saman@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Test 3: Get Profile Before Update
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_2]
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Test 4: Update Own Profile - Success
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/[USER_ID_FROM_TEST_3]
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_2]
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Saman",
  "lastName": "Perera Updated",
  "phone": "+94711234567",
  "address": "123 Main Street",
  "city": "Colombo",
  "state": "WP",
  "postalCode": "00100",
  "country": "Sri Lanka"
}

###

### Test 5: Get Profile After Update
GET http://localhost:3001/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_2]
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Test 6: Partial Update - Only Phone and Address
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/[USER_ID_FROM_TEST_3]
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_2]
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+94722234567",
  "address": "456 Oak Avenue"
}

###

### Test 7: Register Second User (For access control testing)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Test 8: Login Second User
POST http://localhost:3001/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Test 9: Try to Update Another User's Profile - Access Denied (HTTP 403)
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/[SAMAN_USER_ID_FROM_TEST_3]
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_8]
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Hacked",
  "lastName": "Profile"
}

###

### Test 10: Update Own Profile - Partial Update (Only firstName)
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/[JOHN_USER_ID_FROM_TEST_8]
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_8]
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Jonathan"
}

###

### Test 11: Update Profile - Validation Error (firstName too short)
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/[USER_ID_FROM_TEST_3]
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_2]
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "A"
}

###

### Test 12: Update Profile - Validation Error (phone too long)
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/[USER_ID_FROM_TEST_3]
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_2]
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+947112345671234567890123"
}

###

### Test 13: Update Profile - No Token (HTTP 401)
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/[USER_ID_FROM_TEST_3]
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "TestName"
}

###

### Test 14: Update Non-Existent User (HTTP 404)
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/550e8400-e29b-41d4-a716-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_2]
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test"
}

###

### Test 15: Update Profile with Empty Fields (Should be ignored)
PUT http://localhost:3001/api/users/[USER_ID_FROM_TEST_3]
Authorization: Bearer [TOKEN_FROM_TEST_2]
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Saman",
  "lastName": "",
  "phone": null,
  "address": "123 Updated St"
}

###

